No. Commands are queued and delivered at-least-once. They apply on your next `Nodrix.poll()`,
which runs your `NODRIX_WRITE` handlers for anything that arrived while you slept:

```cpp
NODRIX_WRITE("interval_min") {
  if (!value.isNull()) sleepMinutes = value.asInt();
}
```

So a command sent during a nap is applied on the next wake, not lost.

